title    Seven Eighths Fusion (groove revision)
composer Claude
about    Revision of the 4-bar 7/8 fusion loop. Same chords, voicings, pad, tempo and 2+2+3 phrasing, with a rewritten groove in drums, bass and keys rhythm.

# Revision for the note "fusion 7 feels lame. keep everything, just the groove".
# Reading: the harmony, voicings, instruments, form and tempo stay as they were.
# What felt lame is the rhythm: every bar was a copy (% three times), the keys
# stabbed the same four spots in every bar, the hat was a flat eighth grid, and
# the bass repeated one figure. Nothing pushed or pulled against the 2+2+3.
# Changes, all rhythmic:
# - Light 16th swing (0.1) so the sixteenth subdivision leans instead of ticking.
# - Hat moves to 16ths with accent / normal / ghost levels; open hat on step 7
#   in bars 2 and 3 to lift into the long 3-group.
# - Snare gets ghost-note chatter and a second backbeat on step 12 (last eighth
#   of the 3-group), so each bar reads K-S / K..S across 2+2+3.
# - Kick varies bar to bar (pickups on steps 3, 6, 13) but keeps the strong hit
#   on 8 and the 3+3-sixteenth split at 11 that marks the 3-group.
# - Bass becomes a syncopated sixteenth line with ghosted octaves and chromatic
#   approach notes into each bar, still landing roots on steps 0 and 8.
# - Keys keep the exact same note stacks but comp off the grid (hits on the
#   "e" and "a" sixteenths, e.g. steps 3, 6, 9, 11) instead of on every group start.
# Grid: tempo counts eighths (240 = quarter 120); 14 sixteenth steps per bar,
# groups at steps 0, 4, 8 (4+4+6).
tempo    240
beats    7
steps    2
swing    0.1

# Unchanged voices; ohat added as part of the kit so the hat can open.
voice keys epiano vol=0.75 pan=-0.25
voice pad strings vol=0.35 pan=0.3
voice bass ebass vol=0.95
voice kick kick vol=0.95
voice snare snare vol=0.8
voice hat hat vol=0.55
voice ohat ohat vol=0.45
voice crash crash vol=0.6

pattern A
# Keys: original voicings (Dm11, Bbmaj13#11 rootless, Gm9, A7alt), new rhythm.
# Bar 4 still lands A7alt on step 8, restruck on 12 with the snare.
keys | F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4? .- F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- | A3+D4+E4+G4- . A3+D4+E4+G4? . A3+D4+E4+G4- . A3+D4+E4+G4? .- A3+D4+E4+G4-- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4? .- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- | Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4? . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5!-- . G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5- |
# Pad: unchanged.
pad  | E5+A5------------- | -------------- | -------------- | -------- F5+Bb5----- |
# Bass: roots on 0 and 8, ghosted octave or 11th/#11 on the "a" of each
# 2-group, approach notes on step 13 (B1 to Bb1, A1 to G1, F#1 to G1).
bass | D2- . D3? A2- . G2? D2- . C3 A2 B1? | Bb1- . Bb2? F2- . E2? Bb1- . A2 F2 A1? | G1- . G2? D2- . F2? G1- . Bb2 A2 F#1? | G1- . D2? G2? F2 D2 . A1!-- . E2? G2 |
kick  | X... .... X..x.. | x... ..x. X..x.. | X... .... X..x.x | x..x ..x. X..... |
snare | ..o. X..o .o..xo | .o.o X..o .oo.x. | ..o. X..o .o..xo | .o.o X.oo X.ooxX |
hat   | Xoxo xoxo Xoxoxo | Xoxo xox. Xoxoxo | Xoxo xox. Xoxoxo | Xoxo xoxo ...... |
ohat  | .... .... ...... | .... ...x ...... | .... ...x ...... | .... .... ...... |
crash | X... .... ...... | _ | _ | _ |

loop A
